er's advertised ",[165,969,929],{}," (same auth +\n",[165,972,175],{},") before the engine finishes the run ",[165,975,976],{},"cancelled",". The same\nsignal fires on ",[160,979,980],{},"auto-termination"," — when an async run hits its\n",[165,983,984],{},"pollTimeoutMs"," or per-task ",[165,987,330],{}," ceiling, the runner POSTs ",[165,990,966],{},"\nto ",[165,993,929],{}," before the engine fails the run, so a timed-out worker stops at\nthe next stage boundary instead of mutating after the ",[165,996,997],{},"failed"," verdict. A worker\nwithout a ",[165,1000,929],{}," is left to finish on its own (legacy stop-polling).",[157,1003,1004,1007,1008,1010,1011,1014,1015,1017,1018,1020],{},[160,1005,1006],{},"Run deadline."," The dispatch request is capped by the task-level ",[165,1009,330],{},"\nwhen it governs: ",[165,1012,1013],{},"timeoutMs: -1"," (the default when omitted) removes the\ntransport timeout entirely (only the engine\u002Fmanual abort stops the run — for\nhour-scale sync tasks), a positive ",[165,1016,330],{}," caps the dispatch at the\ndeadline. Poll requests keep their own short transport guard (the run duration\nis bounded by the task deadline \u002F engine ",[165,1019,984],{},", not by poll latency).",[1022,1023,1024],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .soVBu, html code.shiki .soVBu{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#999999;--shiki-dark:#666666}html pre.shiki code .s4Jsk, html code.shiki .s4Jsk{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#99841877;--shiki-dark:#B8A96577}html pre.shiki code .sLorS, html code.shiki .sLorS{--shiki-light:#9C3EDA;--shiki-default:#998418;--shiki-dark:#B8A965}html pre.shiki code .sbYkP, html code.shiki .sbYkP{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#B5695977;--shiki-dark:#C98A7D77}html pre.shiki code .sTbE_, html code.shiki .sTbE_{--shiki-light:#91B859;--shiki-default:#B56959;--shiki-dark:#C98A7D}html pre.shiki code .s8XtY, html code.shiki .s8XtY{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#1E754F;--shiki-dark:#4D9375}html pre.shiki 